-- title:
--   Cotangent-length inequality at the localised Hecke algebra, p=3
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $p = 3$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$ which is a semistable model (no prime dividing $\Delta_W$ divides $c_4$) and whose $p$-torsion representation is irreducible (the $p$-torsion of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is nontrivial and has no Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodule other than $0$ and everything). Assume $W$ is residually modular of level $M_0 \geq 1$: there are a normalised weight-$2$ eigenform $f$ on $\Gamma_0(M_0)$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ containing $p$ with $a_\ell(f) \equiv a_\ell(W) \bmod \mathfrak{m}$ for every prime $\ell \neq p$ of good reduction not dividing $M_0$; assume moreover that if $p^2 \mid M_0$ then every $p$-torsion point of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixed by the whole inertia subgroup of some valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its nonunits vanishes, and that $q^3 \nmid M_0$ for every prime $q \neq p$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field and $p$ in its maximal ideal. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$ and every prime dividing $\Delta_W$, and let $N \geq 1$ be such that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$, every $q \in S$ with $q \neq p$ satisfies $q^2 \mid N$ and $q^3 \nmid N$, and at $p$: if $W$ has bad reduction at $p$ or $p \nmid a_p(W)$ then $p \mid N$ and $p^2 \nmid N$, while if $W$ has good reduction at $p$ and $p \mid a_p(W)$ then $p \nmid N$; weight-$2$ level-$N$ cusp forms are assumed to have an integral structure. Finally let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$) to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, with $\theta(T_\ell) = a_\ell(W) \bmod \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ for all primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$. The assertion is that there exists a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}'$ of characteristic zero with finite residue field, finite over $\mathcal{O}$ via an injective local algebra structure map, together with an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra homomorphism $\pi_T$ from the localised Hecke algebra $T =$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪' θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) (the localisation of the $\mathcal{O}'$-base-changed Hecke lattice at the complement of the prime determined by $\theta' = \theta$ followed by the residue-field map of $\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}'$) to $\mathcal{O}'$, such that for every proof that the $p$-torsion of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ has cardinality $p^2$ and that its mod-$p$ Galois representation factors through a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, for every ring homomorphism $\iota$ from $\mathbb{Z}/p$ to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}'$, and for every Hecke–Galois representation datum $H$ on $T$ (a Hecke homomorphism into $T$ lifting $\theta'$, generating $T$ over $\mathcal{O}'$, satisfying the interpolation property for characters, together with a two-dimensional adic Galois representation whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes outside $N$ and $S$ are $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible), the following two inequalities hold. First, if $W$ has bad reduction at $p$ or $p \nmid a_p(W)$, then for every deformation ring datum $D$ for the residual representation $\overline{\rho}_{W,p}$ base-changed along $\iota$ with respect to the ordinary condition over $\mathcal{O}'$ at $p$ outside $S$ (cyclotomic determinant, ordinary at $p$, unramified outside $S$), and every local $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : D.R \to T$ such that the base change of $D.\rho$ along $\varphi$ is equivalent to $H.\rho$, one has $\operatorname{length}_{\mathcal{O}'}$ of the cotangent module of $\ker(\pi_T \circ \varphi)$ at most $\operatorname{length}_{\mathcal{O}'}$ of $\mathcal{O}'$ modulo the image under $\pi_T$ of the annihilator of $\ker \pi_T$. Second, the same inequality holds with the flat condition in place of the ordinary one, under the hypotheses that $W$ has good reduction at $p$ and $p \mid a_p(W)$.
--
--   This is the numerical inequality of the Taylor–Wiles method at the localised Hecke algebra: the cotangent module of the augmentation ideal of the deformation ring, pushed to the Hecke side, is bounded by the congruence module of the Hecke eigenform, in the semistable residually modular situation with $p = 3$ and with the auxiliary level cube-free away from $p$. It is used in the step producing a finite extension of the coefficient ring carrying a Hecke–Galois representation datum and a patching datum, on the way to the modularity of semistable elliptic curves.
